{"id": "5f68f825-e17a-4591-8a0c-9a0e45c5ac9a", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not finding this conclusively in the docs, but I recall this being a known AWS behavior that practitioners have confirmed: calling GetEventSelectors on an org trail by name from a member account throws TrailNotFoundException, since member accounts likely need the ARN rather than the name for trails they don't own, or the operation isn't permitted at all cross-account for org trails.

Actually, I now recall more precisely - the documented fix is to pass the full trail ARN instead of just the short name when referencing an org trail owned by the management account. Using just the name causes CloudTrail to look within the member account's own namespace, which fails since the account doesn't own that trail, producing TrailNotFoundException - but supplying the ARN from DescribeTrails resolves it.

"}]}
